--- a/distribution/tests/require-nonroot/kyverno-test.yaml
+++ b/distribution/tests/require-nonroot/kyverno-test.yaml
@@ -1,42 +1,92 @@
-# Coexistence + self-scoping matrix, offline (`kyverno test`).
-# Each version judges ONLY the pods that claim it; the other version's pods and
-# the unversioned pod are `skip` (out of scope) — proving matchConditions
-# self-scoping and side-by-side coexistence with no shared-webhook collision.
-#
-# 2026-09-04 (ticket 63): the subjects are the two DECLARED lines, 4.0.0 and
-# 5.0.0. They were 2.0.0 and 3.0.0, which the 2026-08-29 retirement deleted from
-# distribution/versions.yaml -- frozen behind their signed tags, delivered to
-# nobody. verify-coexistence.sh now asserts that the `policies:` list below is
-# exactly that declared array, so this file cannot drift back onto retired
-# bodies and go on passing about nothing.
-#
-# 2026-09-24: 4.0.0 is retired from distribution/versions.yaml (owner-instructed),
-# so the `policies:` list is 5.0.0 alone. The pod-4-* rows stay as stragglers: a
-# pod still claiming the retired 4.0.0 is judged by no served require-nonroot, so
-# 5.0.0 must SKIP it. With one declared line this matrix proves self-scoping, not
-# coexistence, and verify-coexistence.sh reads could-not-look for the beat.
 apiVersion: cli.kyverno.io/v1alpha1
 kind: Test
 metadata:
